<title>USA: Sears approached Hechinger on sale - report.</title>
<headline>Sears approached Hechinger on sale - report.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co. recently approached U.S. home improvement retailer Hechinger Co about a possible sale, the Washington Times newspaper reported in Wednesday editions.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted industry sources as saying Sears appeared to be Hechinger's partner in talks which the company said on Tuesday may result in its acquisition for $3.00 a share.</p>
<p>Hechinger, which operates 117 stores in 21 states and the District of Columbia, announced the merger talks on Tuesday but did not identify a potential buyer.</p>
